WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:38.620
[Music]

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.740
[Narrator:] For Helen Roberts, public health nurse,

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.280
it began like any other case:

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.440
a school referral.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.740
An eight-year-old named George Hargrove needed an eye check.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.660
[Music]

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.640
Hardly a relaxed type, this Mrs. Hargrove.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.320
She's young and she's troubled.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.500
But she says George already has an eye appointment,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.060
and that's all that matters.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:16.200
Or is that really all, where you as a public health nurse are concerned?

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:25.380
[Music]

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.220
[Loud crash in other room.]

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:26.860
[Mark:] Ow!

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.180
[Mark crying.]

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.960
[Music]

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.240
[Narrator:] Now who might this young man be?

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:42.740
[Music]

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.840
Could he have anything to do with his mother's

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.420
worn, weary, discouraged look?

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.840
Don't worry, Mrs. Hargrove, all children fall sometimes.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.080
Only Mrs. Hargrove doesn't seem to see it that way.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.080
Mrs. Hargrove is tired and heartsick.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.460
She's exhausted all her own resources.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:13.700
[Music]

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.440
[Mrs. Hargrove:] Don't expect him to say anything, Miss Roberts.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.280
He can't talk.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.060
And that flashlight,

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.580
if you're trying to make some kind of test or something,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.680
you're just wasting your time.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.580
Mark, well, he's awfully slow about everything.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:44.340
[Music]

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.340
[Narrator:] It's terrible for Mrs. Hargrove,

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.620
watching him, hearing the things people say...

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.680
But she still can't believe he's really hopeless,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.920
because you see, she loves her little son.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.300
If only she could see a little progress.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.960
If only he could learn even the simplest things,

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.600
like how to dress himself.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:12.760
Hope, learning, progress, that's where you'll come in, Miss Roberts.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.320
From you, Mrs. Hargrove can learn the importance

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.820
of having Mark tested, diagnosed, evaluated...

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.840
finding out how much he's able to learn.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.600
She needs your emotional support,

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.560
your guidance...

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.440
needs you to help her understand

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:37.060
how much patience and love and ingenuity

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.460
and effort go into teaching a retarded child.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.240
So you're the one to show her

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.180
how to help her child to learn.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:50.980
You, Helen Roberts, public health nurse.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.860
But that's all a long-term project.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.760
And right now, you've a child health record entry to make.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.020
Detailed observations of behavior to note.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.400
Too, you'll have to arrange a referral

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.180
on this case through proper channels.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.300
Draw on your knowledge of state and community resources

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.800
for care of the mentally retarded.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:15.120
See to it that Mark and his parents get all available help

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.900
in dealing with their problem.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:23.860
Ordinarily, each nurse will have at least a few retarded children

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.680
in her caseload.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.420
So sooner or later,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.420
you'll be working with a retarded child.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.440
Often the startle pattern is a good indicator.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.780
Check further when a child doesn't react to a sudden noise.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:42.440
A normal child ordinarily shows a marked response.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.920
Too, a normal child may be expected to track bright objects

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.300
with his eyes at an early age.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:57.780
[Music]

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.440
He doesn't sit passive like this baby.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.240
Such simple tests as these--

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.320
you already know many of them out of your training and experience--

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.060
they all help you to tell the normal child from the retarded.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:16.220
When a five-year-old fails to work a two-year level puzzle,

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.360
it may indicate retardation.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.580
A six-year-old should be able to talk intelligibly.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.120
If he can't, the problem may be a speech defect,

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.720
or it may be retardation.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.760
On the other hand,

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.550
a mother may claim that her child is a behavior problem,

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.790
and try to hide the fact that he's slow

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.910
or emotionally disturbed.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:44.070
[Music]

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.060
In either case, as in all such situations,

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.200
your first step is to call the case to medical attention.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.660
This case-finding is one of a nurse's biggest jobs

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.640
where mental retardation is concerned.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.340
Because retardation has many, many causes:

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.320
brain injury, mongolism

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:10.860
cretinism, galactosemia, prenatal factors,

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.540
familial and dozens of others.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.280
With early diagnosis, some cases can be helped medically.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.680
But all parents can be helped.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.740
to help their youngsters to develop the skills and graces

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.820
they need to live acceptably with others at their level of readiness.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.900
Take feeding.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:33.060
Often, retarded children use a four-finger grip,

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.960
having trouble handling a spoon.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.920
Opposition of the thumb hasn't yet developed.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.240
Sometimes a bent spoon with a padded handle helps.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:46.660
It's easier for the child to use than one that's straight.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.580
It puts his hand in position to grip properly.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:53.200
At first of course, the child may reject the bent spoon.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.840
So you have to impress the mother

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.120
with the necessity for patience.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.580
First you show the mother how to proceed,

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.340
then let her show the child.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:28.730
[Music]

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:30.010
No luck?

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.980
Then go back to the old spoon.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.000
And try to teach the child to grip it with his fist.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:42.520
[Music]

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.540
Sometimes the answer is finger-feeding.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.420
[Music]

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:52.460
Teaching the child to drink from a glass helps, too.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.900
But do limit yourself to showing the mother what to do.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.940
Let her teach the child.

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:14.160
[Music]

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.140
If the child rejects one drink,

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:18.100
offer him another.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.400
The change may help to overcome his negative attitude.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:35.740
[Music]

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.480
Repetition, relaxation, and routine.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.020
These are the three Rs of the retarded.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.140
Together they add up to the kind of help that counts.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:52.020
[Music]

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.920
Toilet problems?

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.520
Take the child to the bathroom on schedule

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.340
and there'll be fewer accidents.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.920
For heaven's sake, leave a lady some privacy!

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:08.920
Oftentimes, play can serve a constructive purpose.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.580
To that end, you carry various items

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.140
for testing and stimulation in your purse.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.780
A rattle, a shiny pencil,

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:31.220
a flashlight, keys that jingle.

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:35.300
You see, we all need reasons for doing things.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.680
So you give young Tom a reason to crawl.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:46.460
[Music]

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.960
Children learn by playing with simple household articles.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.980
They enjoy it, too.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:57.780
[Music]

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.840
This is more than just clipping clothespins to a can.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:04.820
This is how Ronald learns to coordinate.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.680
Using familiar objects in a real-life situation.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:16.460
[Music]

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:19.320
Practical jobs help, too.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.720
As the child masters the skill,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:26.160
she grows in pride, achievement, and usefulness.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.940
The higher-level retarded child

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.700
can become independent and self-supporting.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:38.920
Social graces are another asset many retarded children can acquire.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.400
The trick is to make a game of it.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.800
That way the child learns and has fun at the same time.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:11:10.360
[Music]

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:14.100
And so it goes, in home after home.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:19.120
But it's not always the retarded child who claims your attention.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:23.780
Most parents worry about his brothers and sisters, too.

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:27.380
What effect does the retarded child have on them?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.260
What will happen in the future?

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:35.100
As a nurse, you need to give the family emotional support.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:38.480
Help the parents to accept the situation realistically.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:45.060
[Music]

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.600
Build their self-confidence

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:50.340
so that they can talk frankly and honestly to their children.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:58.180
Every time you show a retarded child genuine love and affection,

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:00.700
you help the mother to become more accepting.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:06.680
Should the child be placed in an institution?

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:10.260
Some youngsters will require such custodial care.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.620
But often parents don't want to give up their child.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.220
And even when the decision is made,

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:19.120
it may take months or years to find a place.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:25.220
In the meanwhile, the family can continue to give loving care,

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.140
and help him to learn what he can.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.240
The physician will discuss the factors

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.300
involved in custodial care as well as care at home.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:41.840
As nurse, it's your job to help the retarded child's parents to understand.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:48.140
Through you, they can come to see the institution

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:51.060
and its function in a truer light.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.060
You can explain how their child may lead

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:57.560
a better, fuller, less complicated life.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:01.480
in a modern public or private school for the retarded.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:05.980
Each retarded child needs a special type of education

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:08.180
geared to his mental age.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:12.900
[Music]

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.980
Starting him to school before he's mentally old enough

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.520
may cause emotional disturbance.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.060
It helps, too, when you introduce families

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:28.120
to their local council of parents for mentally-retarded children.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:31.780
Give them a chance to discover that they are not alone.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:34.220
That others share their problem.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:38.160
Equally important, you are not alone either.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:43.580
Working together, you and the family physician can screen many retardation cases,

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:47.500
though of course it helps if you have a psychologist available to assist you.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:54.200
In Mark's situation, Miss Roberts' first step is to discuss the case with the Hargroves' physician.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:04.440
The community is one of the fortunate few where there's a first-class clinic available.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:08.440
So, the physician refers Mark Hargrove's case there.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:13.100
Here, psychologists evaluate the mental ability of each child,

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:20.180
assist in planning for the youngster's present and his future.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:31.440
A child-development specialist checks educational and social abilities,

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.340
and counsels parents.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:39.040
[Music]

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:44.200
Physical therapists investigate muscle development and physical coordination.

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:54.140
Speech therapists evaluate speech and hearing abilities;

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.220
recommend therapy when indicated.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:05.020
Occupational therapists give practical training in everyday tasks.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:08.060
The social worker studies family relationships

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:13.440
and helps the family use community resources according to their needs.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:18.500
Physicians weigh each individual case and diagnose it.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:22.720
Make decisions, consider treatment.

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:25.480
Intake clinics consult with the parents

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:28.180
and make a preliminary investigation of the case.

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:38.720
[Music]

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:43.940
All these contacts tie together, even more tightly, at staff meetings.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:48.860
When the time comes to staff Mark Hargrove,

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:52.980
Miss Roberts contributes information and opinion,

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:55.440
helps with the evaluation,

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:59.440
raises the question of Mark's readiness.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.980
From a developmental standpoint,

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.980
is he really able to dress himself at this time?

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:21.880
[Music]

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:26.480
Later, the physician summarizes the evaluation from Miss Roberts;

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:36.140
advises her as to how to proceed.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:40.080
A meeting between the physician and Mr. and Mrs. Hargrove

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:45.180
gives them a clear picture of the medical and emotional aspects of Mark's case.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:51.260
It's important that both father and mother be present.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.380
The social worker helps them understand

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:59.000
the broader implications of the situation.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:05.640
The public health nurse in turn has continuing contact with the total family.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:09.340
So Miss Roberts decides to work on Mark's dressing problem

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:13.880
with repetition, relaxation, and routine.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:18.680
She helps Mrs. Hargrove set up a pattern for Mark to follow:

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:23.800
pants, shirt, socks, shoes.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:28.360
Let him put them on in that order every time.

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:34.760
Pants with boxer-type waists are easiest for a child to handle.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:18:02.740
[Music]

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.500
She shows Mrs. Hargrove how to teach Mark

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:08.520
to put on his shirt and button it.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:19.880
[Music]

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:24.000
Putting on a sock involves definite procedures.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.940
It's best to roll it to the toe and work it up the foot,

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.820
clear past the heel.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:48.660
[Music]

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:52.600
The white stripe here goes right across the toes.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:59.460
[Music]

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:01.160
Shoes come next,

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.220
but learning is a slow process for Mark,

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:07.680
so patience is ever the watchword.

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:10.760
The same patience and organized effort

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.240
that helps her in all her work.

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:16.140
By adhering to such organized procedures,

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:18.020
the nurse finds new cases.

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:22.240
She uses all available facilities.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:25.900
She makes proper referrals.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:29.160
She helps with case evaluation.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:33.200
She gives emotional support to anxious parents.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:38.260
Above all she looks for signs of readiness in the child.

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:42.520
She shows his parents how to help him learn.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.780
How long will that learning take?

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.380
How far can he go?

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.820
Nobody knows.

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:54.060
The important thing is to start where he is and then keep trying.

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:56.660
Don't force.

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:59.680
Go at the child's pace.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.840
Don't push.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.700
Your guides are the small goals.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:10.720
[Music]

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.920
In learning to dress himself,

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:16.000
Mark is achieving such a goal.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:20.000
It's one of the few advances he'll ever know, perhaps.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.600
But it's an important one in making life easier

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.820
for him and those about him.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:38.160
[Music]

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.620
His mother is happy that her child has shown the ability to learn,

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:44.040
at least a little.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.080
And with that knowledge comes new hope

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:49.860
for his mastery of other living skills and social graces.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:53.300
His world has changed.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:21:43.100
[Music]

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:45.000
And our Miss Roberts...

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.200
Where does she stand?

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:49.580
She and every other public health nurse

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.640
who has helped a family meet this problem?

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:56.380
Could it be that she feels an even greater satisfaction than the mother?

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:59.780
That in this small triumph,

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:03.720
she sees the proof that her work is truly worthwhile.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:08.000
The justification for all her pride and her profession?

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:11.360
The fulfillment of her ideal of service?

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:14.580
Good questions those, aren't they?

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:18.920
Even though, for public health nurses, they don't need any answers.

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:51.020
[Music]

